    &gt;eclipse-sumo/sumo&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs&#34;&gt;&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;img width=50% src=&#34;https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eclipse/sumo/main/docs/web/docs/images/sumo-logo.svg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;eclipse-sumo---simulation-of-urban-mobility&#34;&gt;Eclipse SUMO - Simulation of Urban MObility
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16268320&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://zenodo.org/badge/DOI/10.5281/zenodo.16268320.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;DOI&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/windows.yml&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/windows.yml/badge.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Windows&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/linux.yml&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/linux.yml/badge.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Linux&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/macos.yml&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/actions/workflows/macos.yml/badge.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;macOS&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sonarcloud.io/summary/overall?id=org.eclipse.sumo&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://sonarcloud.io/api/project_badges/measure?project=org.eclipse.sumo&amp;amp;metric=security_rating&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;sonarcloud security&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/eclipse-sumo/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://hosted.weblate.org/widgets/eclipse-sumo/-/svg-badge.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Translation status&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;img src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/repo-size/eclipse/sumo.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Repo Size&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-sumo&#34;&gt;What is SUMO
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&amp;ldquo;Simulation of Urban MObility&amp;rdquo; (SUMO)&lt;/a&gt; is an open source,
highly portable, microscopic traffic simulation package designed to handle
large road networks and different modes of transport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;&lt;img width=70% src=&#34;https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eclipse/sumo/main/docs/web/docs/images/multiple-screenshots.png&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is mainly developed by employees of the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.dlr.de/ts/en/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Institute of Transportation Systems
at the German Aerospace Center&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;where-to-get-it&#34;&gt;Where to get it
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can download SUMO via our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Downloads.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;downloads site&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the program is still under development (and is being extended continuously), we advice you to
use the latest sources from our GitHub repository. Using a command line client,
execute the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git clone --recursive https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;contact&#34;&gt;Contact
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To stay informed, we have a mailing list for SUMO, which
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://dev.eclipse.org/mailman/listinfo/sumo-user&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;you can subscribe&lt;/a&gt; to.
Messages to the list can be sent to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:sumo-user@eclipse.org&#34; &gt;sumo-user@eclipse.org&lt;/a&gt;.
SUMO announcements will be made through the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:sumo-announce@eclipse.org&#34; &gt;sumo-announce@eclipse.org&lt;/a&gt; list;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://dev.eclipse.org/mailman/listinfo/sumo-announce&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;you can subscribe&lt;/a&gt; to it as well.
For further contact information, have a look at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Contact.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;build-and-installation&#34;&gt;Build and Installation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;For Windows we provide pre-compiled binaries and CMake files to generate Visual Studio projects.
If you want to develop under Windows, please also clone the dependent libraries using:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git clone --recursive https://github.com/DLR-TS/SUMOLibraries
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re using Linux, you should have a look whether your distribution already contains sumo.
There is also a &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://launchpad.net/~sumo&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ppa for ubuntu users&lt;/a&gt; and an
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://build.opensuse.org/project/show/science:dlr&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;open build service instance&lt;/a&gt;.
If you want to build SUMO yourself, the steps for ubuntu are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-gdscript3&#34; data-lang=&#34;gdscript3&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;SUMO_DIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# please insert the correct directory name here&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;SUMO_HOME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;$PWD&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;sudo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;apt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;get&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;cat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build_config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build_req_deb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;txt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build_config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;tools_req_deb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;txt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;cmake&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;cmake&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;--&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;build&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;j&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;nproc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Developer/Main.html#build_instructions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;detailed build instructions, have a look at our Documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;getting-started&#34;&gt;Getting started
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To get started with SUMO, take a look at the docs/tutorial and examples directories,
which contain some example networks with routing data and configuration files.
There is also user documentation provided in the docs/ directory and on the
homepage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The main documentation is at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;sumo.dlr.de/docs&lt;/a&gt;. Note that this tracks the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/FAQ.html#why_does_sumo_not_behave_as_documented_in_this_wiki&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;development version&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mirror of the main documentation is at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.sourceforge.net/docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;sumo.sourceforge.net/docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An offline version of the documentation is part of every release and can be accessed via &lt;code&gt;docs/userdoc/index.html&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;improving-sumo&#34;&gt;Improving SUMO
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Please use the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/eclipse-sumo/sumo/issues&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GitHub issue tracking tool&lt;/a&gt; for bugs and requests,
or file them to the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:sumo-user@eclipse.org&#34; &gt;sumo-user@eclipse.org&lt;/a&gt; list. Before
filing a bug, please consider to check with a current repository checkout
whether the problem has already been fixed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome patches, pull requests and other contributions! For details see &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;CONTRIBUTING.md&#34; &gt;our contribution guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://hosted.weblate.org/projects/eclipse-sumo/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Weblate for translating SUMO&lt;/a&gt;. If you
want to add translation strings or a language, see &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;CONTRIBUTING.md#translating&#34; &gt;our contribution guidelines&lt;/a&gt; and
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Developer/Translating.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;this page&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;license&#34;&gt;License
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;SUMO is licensed under the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://eclipse.org/legal/epl-v20.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Eclipse Public License Version 2&lt;/a&gt;.
The licenses of the different libraries and supplementary code information are in the
subdirectories and in the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://sumo.dlr.de/docs/Libraries_Licenses.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
